# Line-ending protection (owner boot-test find 2026-09-02): Git for
# Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites text files to
# CRLF at checkout — and a CRLF shell script or mounted config breaks the
# moment a Linux container executes it (bash dies on `pipefail\r`; the
# compose db-init and gateway config are bind-mounted straight into
# containers). Pin LF on every file a Linux runtime consumes directly, so
# a PowerShell clone boots identically to a Linux clone.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.sql       text eol=lf
*.conf      text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.toml      text eol=lf
Dockerfile* text eol=lf
.env.example    text eol=lf
selfhost.env.example text eol=lf
